s</strong>, close to the 116 that chance alone would give, and <strong>169 record highs</strong>, more than the 116 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (71). Cold Bay's all-time high is 78\u00b0F, on August 22, 1948.","t_chg":"Cold Bay has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 80 complete years: Cold Bay's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.43), about +2.3\u00b0F since 1943. Cold Bay's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.48\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.34 to +0.62), about +3.9\u00b0F since 1943.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Cold Bay has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Cold Bay's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.49 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.68 to +2.31), about +12.2 inches since 1943. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 42.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 2000 (84.32 in); the driest, 1950 (20.80 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 10 daily record highs, 7 daily record lows"}}